  "segments": [
    {
      "text": "Everyone says Brahma, the creator, made the first humans, but Brahma could not do it. His own sons had rejected him, and creation was wearing him down. So who showed him how? The one god he believed could not create. Vishnu, the preserver, noticed Brahma's grief. He told him to go to Mahadev, another name for Shiva. Brahma said the destroyer could not create. Vishnu said Shiva might not create, but he would surely counsel. Brahma found Shiva meditating. He sat down and prayed from the depth of his soul. Shiva opened his eyes. He said reproduction could not happen the way Brahma had made his sons. What Brahma needed was Shakti, the power of the feminine. Then Shiva's body changed. The right side became male, the left side became female, split evenly down the middle. This form was called Ardhanarishvara, the androgynous one. Shiva said masculine and feminine were the two halves of the cosmos. Neither could work without the other. Brahma bowed to the goddess and asked to create the female. She gave him the generative force. From his own body, Brahma made a man named Manu and a woman named Brahmi. The human race descends from Manu. The destroyer had not made the first humans. He had shown the creator what creation needed, both halves.",
      "start_time": 0.16,
      "end_time": 79.44,
